  notes: |
    T1 of wavecode-ui-design-overhaul coordinator. Three user-visible bugs
    fixed in one commit (174 LoC):

    1. Piano CSS-scope: `.piano-key.black/white/active` in legacy.css
       renamed to `.piano-keyboard .piano-key.*` so components.css
       (loaded earlier) wins cascade for the new PianoKeyboard component.
       Bug was: black keys fell out of piano (rendered after all whites
       because legacy.css's `position: relative; flex: 0 0 22px` overrode
       components.css's `position: absolute`).

    2. MiniNotationToolbar reactivity: ScorePanel passes
       `editor={() => editorApi}` (accessor) instead of
       `editor={editorApi}` (let-binding). Toolbar reads
       `props.editor?.()?.getView()`. Bug was: clicks did nothing
       because toolbar started with `editor=undefined` and Solid
       didn't reactively re-render.

    3. Toolbar visibility: `.mini-toolbar { flex-shrink: 0;
       margin-top: auto }` inside flex-column. NOT position: sticky
       (would break under overflow:hidden parent). Bug was: toolbar
       hidden behind cm-host flex:1 + bottom-sheet overlap.

    Tests: 22/22 pass (9 PianoKeyboard incl. 5 layout invariants +
    13 MiniNotationToolbar incl. 3 click-with-EditorView). tsc clean.
    vite build OK after `npm install` in worktree (pnpm's symlink
    layout breaks Rollup resolution for transitive superdough — note
    for T2-T5 worktree setup).

    Renamed MiniNotationToolbar.test.ts → .tsx because vitest/esbuild
    refuses JSX in .ts files.